      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village’s oldest house, the Cook House, dates to the turn of the 19th century and features a distinctive partial brick gable end.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://apps.mht.maryland.gov/nr/NRDetail.aspx?NRID=1113",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fairmount is surrounded by the Annemessex, Manokin, and Back Creek rivers, with Tangier Sound forming its western boundary.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://apps.mht.maryland.gov/nr/NRDetail.aspx?NRID=1113",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Two churches and two general stores have stood in Fairmount for generations, reflecting its modest, agrarian character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://apps.mht.maryland.gov/nr/NRDetail.aspx?NRID=1113",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
